      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "YOLO instance segmentation, rebuilt from GENERIC cv2.dnn nodes\n\nMirrors the YOLO26-seg reference pipeline (huggingface.co/opencv/opencv_contribution) with NO model-specific monolith (contrast the all-in-one 'CV YOLOv4 Detect' node). The 'YOLO-Seg Inference' subgraph decomposes the pipeline:\n\n  DNN Letterbox        (aspect-preserving resize + 114 pad to 640)\n  DNN Blob From Image  (scale 1/255, BGR->RGB)\n  DNN Forward All      (loads yolo26n-seg.onnx, returns BOTH outputs)\n  DNN Pick Output x2   (the (1,300,38) detection head + the (1,32,160,160) mask prototypes, picked by shape; 'by name' also available so output ORDER does not matter)\n  YOLO Detect Decode   (unwraps boxes/scores/class ids; the layout dropdown also covers yolov5/v8 class-score heads and yolov4 separate boxes+confs)\n  YOLO Seg Masks       (OPTIONAL second stage: one binary MASK per detection from the kept rows' mask coefficients @ proto, crop, upsample, un-letterbox)\n\nClass names are NOT baked in: 'CV Load Labels' reads example_inputs/coco-labels-2014_2017.txt (line N = class id N) and feeds the decoder. To adapt to another model: swap the model combo + layout dropdown inside the subgraph (detection-only models just delete/bypass the 'YOLO Seg Masks' node). Put yolo26n-seg.onnx in the models/onnx folder (.tflite models are listed too, but OpenCV's TFLite importer rejects this particular one - use the ONNX export instead). Boxes go to the core 'Draw BBoxes' node, masks to 'Overlay Masks'. Zero detections is a valid result (found=false, empty outputs)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
